{"name":"Peppergrass","hex":"#767461","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"peppergrass","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the pungent herbs of the cruciferous genus Lepidium, especially the garden peppergrass, or garden cress, Lepidium sativum","The pillwort, or European pillwort (Pilularia globulifera)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peppergrass"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lepidium","blocks":[{"text":"Lepidium is a genus of plants in the mustard/cabbage family, Brassicaceae. The genus is widely distributed in the Americas, Africa, Asia, Europe, and Australia. It includes familiar species such as garden cress, maca, and dittander. General common names include peppercress, peppergrass, pepperweed, and pepperwort. Some species form tumbleweeds.\nThe genus name Lepidium is from Greek meaning 'small scale', which is thought to be derived from a folk medicine usage of the plant to treat leprosy, which cause small scales on the skin. Another meaning is related to the small scale-like fruit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Lepidium_flavum_3.jpg/330px-Lepidium_flavum_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lepidium","wikidata":"Q146217"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Cakile_maritima_habitat.jpg/500px-Cakile_maritima_habitat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Cakile_maritima_habitat.jpg/1280px-Cakile_maritima_habitat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Cakile_maritima_habitat.jpg/500px-Cakile_maritima_habitat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lepidium latifolium on the Kattegat","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/F